@node Commands
@chapter Commands

@section inspect

@command{maize inspect} reports the selected kernel configuration, hardware
inventory, Gentoo snapshot, known recommendations, and unresolved package
kernel policy. Use @option{--verbose} to show every unresolved finding.

@section generate

@command{maize generate} requires @option{--kernel-tree} and @option{--output}.
It applies known recommendations, delegates dependency resolution to the
target kernel's Kconfig evaluator, verifies required decisions, and writes the
validated configuration atomically.

@section migrate

With no artifact arguments, @command{maize migrate} loads the running kernel
configuration, discovers versioned source trees below @file{/usr/src}, selects
the newest kernel release, and resolves the running configuration through that
target tree. The report names both releases and paths. Supplying all four
old/new Kconfig and configuration options retains explicit artifact comparison.
The text report groups lost and newly enabled capabilities, built-in/module
transitions, other value changes, and inactive symbol churn. Large groups are
capped unless @option{--verbose} is supplied. Contextual JSON uses the
@code{maize.migration/v3} contract and includes every classified change.

@section check

@command{maize check} checks known required capabilities. A result is
indeterminate when unresolved package kernel policy remains, even if there are
no known missing recommendations.

@section impact

@command{maize impact --config @var{path}} currently reports known
requirements that the proposed configuration does not satisfy.
Consumer-oriented package and hardware consequence reporting remains under
development.

@section observe

@command{maize observe --output @var{path}} writes a versioned JSON hardware
inventory.

@node Output
@chapter Output

Text output is colored only when appropriate for the destination terminal.
@option{--color auto} is the default. @option{--color always} forces ANSI
color and @option{--color never} disables it. The @env{NO_COLOR} environment
variable disables automatic color. JSON never contains ANSI escape sequences.

Concise output groups unresolved package policy by category and package count.
Use @option{--verbose} when the individual ebuild and eclass findings are
needed.

@node Kernel validation
@chapter Kernel validation

Maize uses the selected target kernel's own Kconfig implementation as the
authority. Validation occurs against a temporary configuration outside the
source tree. Required decisions that Kconfig removes or weakens cause
generation to fail before the output path is created or replaced.

@node Exit status
@chapter Exit status

@table @code
@item 0
Success. For @command{check}, known requirements are satisfied.
@item 1
Execution or validation failed.
@item 2
Invalid command-line usage.
@item 3
@command{check} found known required changes.
@item 4
@command{check} is indeterminate because package policy remains unresolved.
@end table

@node Bash completion
@chapter Bash completion

Source @file{completions/maize.bash} from an interactive Bash startup file, or
install it in the system Bash completion directory. It completes commands,
options, enum values, files, and directories.

@node Safety
@chapter Safety

Inspection and analysis are read-only. Output-producing commands require an
explicit destination and use atomic replacement. Kernel validation does not
modify the selected source tree. Maize never shells out to package-querying
tools; Gentoo package state is consumed through Gentooling Go APIs.

@bye
